{"name":"Sour Patch Peach","hex":"#f4d9c5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of acidity.","Made rancid by fermentation, etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sensation of a sour taste.","A drink made with whiskey, lemon or lime juice and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sour"},{"term":"patch","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of cloth, or other suitable material, sewed or otherwise fixed upon a garment to repair or strengthen it, especially upon an old garment to cover a hole.","A small piece of anything used to repair damage or a breach; as, a patch on a kettle, a roof, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To mend by sewing on a piece or pieces of cloth, leather, or the like.","To mend with pieces; to repair by fastening pieces on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/patch"},{"term":"peach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of species Prunus persica, native to China and now widely cultivated throughout temperate regions, having pink flowers and edible fruit.","Soft juicy stone fruit of the peach tree, having yellow flesh, downy, red-tinted yellow skin, and a deeply sculptured pit or stone containing a single seed."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the color peach.","Particularly pleasing or agreeable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sour Patch Kids","blocks":[{"text":"Sour Patch Kids are a brand of soft gummy candy with a coating of invert sugar and sour sugar. The tartaric and citric acids provide the candy with a sharp burst of tartness, while the inverted sugar gives the soft gummy its sweet flavor. Sour Patch Kids Extreme, which contains malic acid in addition to the tartaric and citric acids, is considered the sourest variation in the Sour Patch line of candies. The slogans \"Sour Then Sweet\" and \"Sour. Sweet. Gone.\" refer to the candy's sour-to-sweet taste.."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Sour-Patch-Kids.jpg/330px-Sour-Patch-Kids.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sour_Patch_Kids"},{"title":"Peach","blocks":[{"text":"The peach is a deciduous tree that bears edible juicy fruits with various characteristics. Most are simply called peaches, while the glossy-skinned, non-fuzzy varieties are called nectarines. Though from the same species, they are regarded commercially as different fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg/330px-Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach"},{"title":"Peach (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Peach is a color that is named for the pale color of the interior flesh of the peach fruit. Like the color apricot, the color peach is paler than most actual peach fruits and seems to have been formulated primarily to create a pastel palette of colors for interior design."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peach_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Sour-Patch-Kids.jpg/500px-Sour-Patch-Kids.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Sour-Patch-Kids.jpg/1280px-Sour-Patch-Kids.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Sour-Patch-Kids.jpg/500px-Sour-Patch-Kids.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASour-Patch-Kids.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Illustration_Prunus_persica_clean_no_descr.